  {
   "id": 544237,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Although there are many different hormones in the human body, they can be divided into three classes based on their chemical structure. Explain these classes and give one factor that distinguishes each.",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1069617,
     "content_html": "The classes are peptide hormones, which are water insoluble, and amino acid-derived and lipid-derived hormones, which are water soluble."
    },
    {
     "id": 1069618,
     "content_html": "The classes are lipid-derived hormones, which are water insoluble, and amino acid-derived and peptide hormones, which are water soluble."
    },
    {
     "id": 1069619,
     "content_html": "The classes are lipid-derived hormones, which are water soluble, and amino acid-derived and peptide hormones, which are water insoluble."
    },
    {
     "id": 1069620,
     "content_html": "The classes are amino acid-derived hormones, which are water insoluble, and lipid-derived and peptide hormones, which are water soluble."
